WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.734
-Yet another former Trump
adviser is out

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:06.033
with a self-serving book about
their time in the White House.

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:08.267
Meanwhile, the committee
investigating the attempted coup

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:10.067
on January 6th interviewed

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:12.634
Trump's former attorney
for more than nine hours.

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:14.634
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:16.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:18.968
♪♪

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:20.901
There have been a flood of books

00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:23.100
from former Trump advisers
since he left office.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.868
And while most of them have been
dishonest and self-serving,

00:00:25.868 --> 00:00:30.000
there's one coming out soon
that I think has the potential

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.667
to be refreshingly candid
and revealing.

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:34.934
And -- oh, wait, never mind.
It's Kellyanne Conway.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.100
-Kellyanne Conway is the author
of a brand-new book,

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.167
"Here's the Deal,"
and she joins us now.

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:41.167
-Sorry, but the person
who famously coined the phrase

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:43.667
"alternative facts" does not
get to cash in on a book,

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:45.901
given that there's not a single
word of it we should believe.

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:47.767
I bet even the cover is a lie.

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:49.234
By Kellyanne Conway?

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:50.467
That probably means
her real name

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:53.234
is something like
Connie Anne Kellyway.

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:55.033
This book is also called
"Here's the Deal,"

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:56.934
which should be
an automatic red flag,

00:00:56.934 --> 00:00:59.200
because usually when someone
says those words,

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.501
they've been caught in a lie.

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:03.100
"Gary, are you sexting
with your co-worker?"

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.200
"What? No. Why?"
"Because in your phone,

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.667
there's a notification
that says you have a new sext."

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:11.834
"Okay, here's the deal."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:15.534
"I thought it was the new iPhone
update, and I had no choice."

00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:18.167
Also isn't "Here's the Deal"
a Joe Biden thing?

00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:21.300
Is she trying to troll us all
by naming her book after a thing

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.067
Joe Biden famously says?

00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:24.467
-Here's the deal.
Here's the deal.

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:25.667
Here's the deal.
Here's the deal.

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:26.767
Here's the deal.
Here's the deal.

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:28.467
Here's the deal.
Here's the deal.

00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:30.634
-What's she gonna call
her next book?

00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:32.234
"Look, Jack,
Get Your Facts Straight,

00:01:32.234 --> 00:01:36.400
C'mon Man: My Time as
Barack Obama's Vice President"?

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:39.734
If you ask me, there's really
only one thing Kellyanne Conway

00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:41.767
should be remembered for --
her snide response

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.334
to a question about COVID

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:46.968
being contained
in March of 2020.

00:01:46.968 --> 00:01:48.300
-You talked about how
the administration

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.601
initially had this contained,
but during that time,

00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:52.601
why didn't the administration
send out more tests

00:01:52.601 --> 00:01:54.200
and work
to get hospitals prepared?

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.200
I mean, even today,
the state of Florida is saying

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:59.100
they can't test everyone per
the administration's guidelines

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.300
because they don't have
enough tests.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.100
-So you're asking a couple
different things there.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.167
I'll try to just
give some facts.

00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:08.667
The HHS secretary said this
morning that we're ramping up.

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:10.067
We're ramping up
with the commercial labs --

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:11.868
-Why now? Why didn't they do it
while it was contained?

00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:12.968
Get ahead of it?

00:02:12.968 --> 00:02:14.434
-It is being contained.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.334
And do you not think
it's being contained?

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:18.067
-Congrats, Kellyanne.
You were right.

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:22.067
It was contained in March 2020.
COVID quickly fizzled out.

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:24.100
Hydroxychloroquine
and horse paste worked,

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.434
and we never heard of it again.

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:27.100
Toilet paper was free
and plentiful.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.801
No one was locked
in their homes for a year.

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:31.667
And I kept doing my show
in a suit and tie with a haircut

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:33.000
and a full, unmasked audience.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.167
That's me from yesterday's show.
It was so good.

00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:36.834
We did "A Closer Look"
about the first year

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:39.300
of Trump's second term
and how he has a 98% approval

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.033
rating after successfully
containing COVID,

00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:43.501
winning the snowboarding
gold medal at the Olympics,

00:02:43.501 --> 00:02:45.267
and wrapping with Dre
and Snoop Dogg

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:47.000
at the Super Bowl halftime show.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.667
♪ My name is Trump,
and I'm here to say ♪

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:50.334
♪ I made COVID go away ♪

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:52.167
Wait, wait, wait.
No, I got that all wrong.

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:54.300
None of that happened, right?
COVID is still raging,

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.767
Trump lost the election,
and I spent a year in lockdown,

00:02:56.767 --> 00:03:00.968
swatting away wasps and growing
out my hair like old Loki.

00:03:00.968 --> 00:03:02.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:05.167
Oh, wait.
Oh, God. Oh, God.

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:07.334
You know what that means?
This has been...

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:10.968
[ Thunder crashes ]

00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:15.167
[ Eerie music plays ]

00:03:15.167 --> 00:03:19.634
Wait. Is this the timeline where
Wally has luscious golden locks?

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:21.234
-You know it, baby!

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:25.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:28.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:33.234
Anyway, I'm not gonna
quote from the book

00:03:33.234 --> 00:03:35.367
because there's no reason
to believe anything in it.

00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:37.400
Conway was such a prolific
and shameless liar

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:40.033
that we shouldn't take a single
thing she says at face value.

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:42.801
In fact, that's how we should
treat anyone in the GOP

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:45.367
who backed Trump's big lie
about non-existent fraud

00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:47.601
in the 2020 election.
Like for some reason,

00:03:47.601 --> 00:03:50.167
news outlets keep inviting
on Republican politicians

00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:52.434
to repeat the brazen
and unhinged lie

00:03:52.434 --> 00:03:54.300
that the 2020 election
was somehow tainted.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:57.100
Yesterday on CBS,
Florida Senator Rick Scott,

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:58.634
who objected
to the certification

00:03:58.634 --> 00:04:01.167
of Pennsylvania's electoral
votes on January 6th,

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:04.434
even after the violent mob
stormed the Capitol,

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:06.901
implied that there was fraud
in the election

00:04:06.901 --> 00:04:08.267
with very little pushback.

00:04:08.267 --> 00:04:10.300
-There is clearly people
that are still concerned

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.000
about what happened in 2020,

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.667
and they would like
the facts to come out.

00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:15.901
And they want
to know what happened...

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:19.067
-What do you mean by that?
-...why it happened.

00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:20.267
Well, they want to know --

00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:22.300
They want to know
that exactly what happened --

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.334
If, you know,
were there problems,

00:04:24.334 --> 00:04:26.033
exactly what happened.

00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:27.467
They'd like to know that.

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:30.868
But also, you know, they also
want to make sure we win in '22.

00:04:30.868 --> 00:04:33.534
So, you know, they they want
to make sure that,

00:04:33.534 --> 00:04:35.734
you know, we're going to make
sure their votes' not diluted.

00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:38.501
So I think you have to -- you
have to talk about, you know,

00:04:38.501 --> 00:04:41.033
making sure people understand
what happened in 2020,

00:04:41.033 --> 00:04:42.467
but also make sure,
you know,

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:44.234
they know that you're going to
focus on making sure

00:04:44.234 --> 00:04:47.400
that 2022 is a -- you know,
is a fair election.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.234
-What do you mean, "They want
to know what happened"?

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:51.334
You know how many audits
and recounts we've had?

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:54.567
Does everyone need to get a turn
going through all the ballots

00:04:54.567 --> 00:04:57.000
with a microscope
so they can personally confirm

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.701
that the 2020 election
was legit?

00:04:58.701 --> 00:04:59.734
"Honey, what's all this?"

00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:01.467
"Oh, they're ballots
from Georgia.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.501
I guess it's my turn
to verify the results."

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:05.701
"But, honey, you don't know
anything about elections."

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:06.868
"That's what I tried
to tell them,

00:05:06.868 --> 00:05:08.968
but they said it was my turn!"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.968 --> 00:05:10.200
We know what happened.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.200
Georgia reaffirmed
Biden's victory three times,

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.367
and even a Republican-sponsored
audit in Arizona,

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:16.701
conducted by a group
called the Cyber Ninjas,

00:05:16.701 --> 00:05:18.534
confirmed Biden's win there.

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:21.868
And if you can't trust a group
called the Cyber Ninjas,

00:05:21.868 --> 00:05:23.534
who can you trust?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.534 --> 00:05:25.934
Cyber Ninjas sounds like
the name of an NFT

00:05:25.934 --> 00:05:27.834
that originally sold
for $10,000

00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:30.601
and now is going
for 5 bucks on eBay.

00:05:30.601 --> 00:05:32.767
Meanwhile, cyber ninja
with an eyepatch

00:05:32.767 --> 00:05:34.367
is now worth like $1,200,000.

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:36.801
And look, I'm not saying I own
the one without an eyepatch.

00:05:36.801 --> 00:05:38.367
I'm just saying,
is the eyepatch one

00:05:38.367 --> 00:05:40.434
really so much better?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.434 --> 00:05:42.133
In fact, the Republican
search for voter fraud

00:05:42.133 --> 00:05:44.801
was such a bust that Texas
Lieutenant Governor Dan Patrick

00:05:44.801 --> 00:05:47.200
offered a reward
for proof of voter fraud.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.334
And one of the very few cases
that surfaced

00:05:49.334 --> 00:05:51.534
was a Republican
in Pennsylvania

00:05:51.534 --> 00:05:53.934
who used his dead mother's
ballot to vote for Trump.

00:05:53.934 --> 00:05:56.267
So Pennsylvania's lieutenant
governor, John Fetterman,

00:05:56.267 --> 00:05:58.033
who just won the Democratic
primary for Senate

00:05:58.033 --> 00:05:59.467
in Pennsylvania last week,

00:05:59.467 --> 00:06:02.200
said at the time that he would
accept Patrick's reward

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:03.801
in the form
of a gift certificate

00:06:03.801 --> 00:06:05.767
to regional convenience store
Sheetz.

00:06:05.767 --> 00:06:08.133
-The fraud that we know
that has occurred

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:09.868
in Pennsylvania in this cycle

00:06:09.868 --> 00:06:14.100
is a registered Republican
in Luzerne County

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:17.734
trying to vote for Trump
with his dead mother's ballot.

00:06:17.734 --> 00:06:20.067
Other than that, no,
we have not witnessed

00:06:20.067 --> 00:06:22.868
any voter fraud
here in Pennsylvania.

00:06:22.868 --> 00:06:27.100
I want my reward.
You know, he wanted voter fraud,

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:30.200
and from one fellow
lieutenant governor to another,

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:34.667
it's like, you know, he can
pay me in a Sheetz gift card.

00:06:34.667 --> 00:06:37.033
That would be fine.
And the bottom line is,

00:06:37.033 --> 00:06:39.334
like, you know,
my dude wants voter fraud?

00:06:39.334 --> 00:06:40.901
I delivered it in Pennsylvania

00:06:40.901 --> 00:06:44.234
because that is the one
lone case of voter fraud

00:06:44.234 --> 00:06:47.067
documented right now,
as of this airing.

00:06:47.067 --> 00:06:49.167
By the way, if you don't know
about Sheetz,

00:06:49.167 --> 00:06:51.400
outside of New York,
it's the only place you can go

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:55.300
to buy mouthwash, fuzzy dice,
a 12-inch sub, and a six pack

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:57.300
of Keystone Light
at the same time.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:59.033
[ Laughter ]
And, yeah, if you want

00:06:59.033 --> 00:07:01.300
to quietly slip
an adult magazine in there,

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:03.234
go for it.
It's not porn!

00:07:03.234 --> 00:07:05.000
Sheetz don't sell porn.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:07.501
It's something tasteful that
you can enjoy with your sub.

00:07:07.501 --> 00:07:09.567
And by the way, I realize
I'm stepping into the middle

00:07:09.567 --> 00:07:12.534
of an extremely fraught rivalry
here between Sheetz and Wawa.

00:07:12.534 --> 00:07:13.801
I have an allegiance
to Pittsburgh,

00:07:13.801 --> 00:07:16.434
but my staff is packed
with people from Jersey,

00:07:16.434 --> 00:07:18.400
Philly, and,
worst of all, Delaware.

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:20.968
They all --
[ Laughter ]

00:07:20.968 --> 00:07:23.334
They all insist
Wawa is better than Sheetz,

00:07:23.334 --> 00:07:25.367
but I'm the host,
so I get to decide.

00:07:25.367 --> 00:07:27.400
And to fans of Wawa,
I simply say...

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.334
[ Wah, wah! ]

00:07:29.334 --> 00:07:33.934
[ Laughter ]

00:07:33.934 --> 00:07:36.501
Anyway, back to Fetterman.
My favorite part of his demand

00:07:36.501 --> 00:07:38.400
that Patrick pay him
the reward money

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:39.901
was a tweet he sent to Patrick

00:07:39.901 --> 00:07:42.234
that ended with,
"P.S. The Cowboys blow."

00:07:42.234 --> 00:07:43.234
[ Laughter ]

00:07:43.234 --> 00:07:44.767
And even if you're
a Cowboys fan,

00:07:44.767 --> 00:07:46.801
you have to admit
he's a man of his convictions,

00:07:46.801 --> 00:07:48.534
because when he asked
about that tweet on CNN,

00:07:48.534 --> 00:07:49.968
he did not back down.

00:07:49.968 --> 00:07:52.934
-Well, let's first establish
the Cowboys do, in fact, blow.

00:07:52.934 --> 00:07:55.067
[ Laughter ]

00:07:55.067 --> 00:07:56.901
-At the end of the day,
this man is a unifier.

00:07:56.901 --> 00:07:59.133
He may have driven a wedge
with this Sheetz endorsement,

00:07:59.133 --> 00:08:00.934
but the whole state
can come together to agree

00:08:00.934 --> 00:08:02.267
that the Cowboys [bleep] blow.

00:08:02.267 --> 00:08:04.701
Also, I appreciate
Fetterman's willingness

00:08:04.701 --> 00:08:06.133
to use football analogies,

00:08:06.133 --> 00:08:08.300
like when he said that demanding
an audit of the election

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:10.133
was the equivalent of demanding
to be

00:08:10.133 --> 00:08:12.434
added to the roster
of the Pittsburgh Steelers.

00:08:12.434 --> 00:08:14.467
-I just want your viewers
to understand that --

00:08:14.467 --> 00:08:15.901
that the people
that are involved

00:08:15.901 --> 00:08:18.067
in these kinds of audits
in Pennsylvania

00:08:18.067 --> 00:08:21.033
are not the sharpest knives
in the GOP drawer.

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:23.067
No one's taking this seriously.

00:08:23.067 --> 00:08:26.100
I could issue a letter
on my office's letterhead

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:29.100
to the Pittsburgh Steelers,
saying, "I demand I be installed

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:32.100
as the starting left tackle
for the upcoming season,"

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:33.968
and that could generate
some new stories,

00:08:33.968 --> 00:08:36.734
but it's not gonna go
anywhere, and neither is this.

00:08:36.734 --> 00:08:39.334
-And this is coming from a guy
who, of all politicians,

00:08:39.334 --> 00:08:41.033
has the best chance
of actually becoming

00:08:41.033 --> 00:08:43.100
the starting left tackle
for the Steelers.

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:44.968
Dude is 6'9".

00:08:44.968 --> 00:08:46.467
But he's certainly
right about one thing.

00:08:46.467 --> 00:08:48.334
The people involved
in these scam audits

00:08:48.334 --> 00:08:50.367
are not the sharpest knives
in the drawer,

00:08:50.367 --> 00:08:52.834
which brings us, of course,
to a straight-up spoon,

00:08:52.834 --> 00:08:55.367
Rudy Giuliani, who --
[ Laughter ]

00:08:55.367 --> 00:08:57.667
who always
looks like he's surprised

00:08:57.667 --> 00:09:00.267
to find out
he's Rudy Giuliani.

00:09:00.267 --> 00:09:01.501
[ Laughter ]

00:09:01.501 --> 00:09:03.701
"Oh, no, not that one, I hope!"

00:09:03.701 --> 00:09:05.634
Rudy looks like
he just challenged Fetterman

00:09:05.634 --> 00:09:07.133
to a bar fight,
and then realized

00:09:07.133 --> 00:09:09.300
how tall Fetterman was
when he stood up.

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:11.601
"Oh, never mind! You can keep
talking to my wife, big guy.

00:09:11.601 --> 00:09:13.667
Besides, she's my cousin.
It's unnatural."

00:09:13.667 --> 00:09:15.100
[ Laughter ]

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:18.067
Anyway, Rudy was, of course,
integral to the failed attempt

00:09:18.067 --> 00:09:20.667
to overturn the results
in various swing states,

00:09:20.667 --> 00:09:22.801
including specifically
in Pennsylvania.

00:09:22.801 --> 00:09:25.367
And as a result, the committee
investigating the coup conducted

00:09:25.367 --> 00:09:28.367
a virtual interview with him
last week that lasted for hours.

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:30.501
-Some big news
from the January 6th committee.

00:09:30.501 --> 00:09:32.667
Tonight, in the past hour,
we have learned

00:09:32.667 --> 00:09:34.501
that President Trump's
personal lawyer,

00:09:34.501 --> 00:09:36.534
former New York Mayor
Rudy Giuliani,

00:09:36.534 --> 00:09:39.167
testified today
before the 1/6 committee.

00:09:39.167 --> 00:09:40.834
NBC News confirms that Giuliani

00:09:40.834 --> 00:09:44.133
testified virtually
for approximately 9 hours.

00:09:44.133 --> 00:09:46.601
-9 hours?
I mean, I guess it makes sense.

00:09:46.601 --> 00:09:49.234
The dude was involved in almost
every aspect of the coup,

00:09:49.234 --> 00:09:50.567
so there's a lot to discuss.

00:09:50.567 --> 00:09:53.133
Either that or he kept
having technical difficulties.

00:09:53.133 --> 00:09:55.567
